  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WILDLIFE CRIME DATABASE: A VITAL TOOL TO STRENGTHEN EFFORTS TO CURB TIGER POACHING AND TRADE, AND RELATED WILDLIFE CRIMES IN INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO REINFORCE NATIONAL EFFORTS TO CURB WILDLIFE CRIME INVOLVING ENDANGERED SPECIES, PARTICULARLY AGAINST TIGERS, ACROSS INDIA. THE PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE TO EFFICIENTLY FACILITATE ENFORCEMENT ACTION AGAINST WILDLIFE CRIME THROUGHOUT INDIA BY GATHERING AND DISSEMINATING AN UPDATED AND SYSTEMATIC DATA ANALYSIS THAT IS UTILIZED TO DISRUPT WILDLIFE CRIMINAL NETWORKS ACROSS INDIA. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE COLLECTING AND VERIFYING RELEVANT LEADS ON WILDLIFE CRIME, UPDATING THE EXISTING DATABASE WITH COUNTRY-WIDE STATISTICS, ANALYZING WILDLIFE CRIME TRENDS USING I2 SOFTWARE, PROVIDING INPUTS AND ASSISTANCE TO ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES, DISSEMINATING INFORMATION TO STRENGTHEN POLICY, AND MONITORING DEVELOPMENT OF THIS EXCLUSIVE DATABASE.</narrative>
  </description>
